    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc939e04_bdf6ec24",
        "filename": "include/core/SkPath.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1953,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T14:03:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m of two minds about the best place to store this.\n\nFiniteness is a property of the geometry/points, so it seems to naturally belong to `SkPathData`.  It takes work to track state in `SkPath` and to ensure we don\u0027t end up with different paths disagreeing about the same pathdata being finite.\n\nOTOH we have that friction where we want to communicate transform failure with a non-finite `Empty` path data, but that\u0027s normally a singleton.  Maybe it wouldn\u0027t be too bad to add another `EmptyNonFinite` factory backed by a separate singleton?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1953,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 1953,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "5d15444797833cfc9cad8fd62d200654aee81292",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4711e60e_2476b3ce",
        "filename": "include/core/SkPath.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 1953,
      "author": {
        "id": 5648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T15:06:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yea, I thought about that (a sentinel pathdata value), just not sure.\n\nWe could also just store nullptr in the SkPath -- that is the clearest (to me) signal of \u0027not having geometry) -- but that\u0027s inconvenient for our impl sites.",
      "parentUuid": "dc939e04_bdf6ec24",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1953,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 1953,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "5d15444797833cfc9cad8fd62d200654aee81292",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
